## Temptation / recall

I recognized Stripe/Collison, Airbnb/Chesky, Phil Knight, Jensen Huang, Hopfield, and Mokyr before I reached them. I did **not** start from those names. They entered only when the walk landed on them, and I did not skip them for being famous. That is the failure mode the brief forbids in both directions.

I was tempted to skip Knight and Huang as “too obvious,” and tempted to skip Bushnell as maybe the same Atari event as Alcorn. I did not skip Knight or Huang. I kept Bushnell because Alcorn was an Atari employee (later own ventures) and Atari is not an existing hit entity.

I did not rebalance by country, era, or sex. This wave is heavily male and US-weighted because that is what the lists produced in order.
